[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605250630-yakushi-wave-1c-r1-chiral-commissioning", :adr/title "yakushi Wave 1c R1 — Chiral synthesis commissioning and benzonatate PMDA jurisdiction", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# yakushi Wave 1c R1 — Chiral synthesis commissioning and benzonatate PMDA jurisdiction\n\n**Date:** 2026-05-25\n**Author:** Jun Kawasaki\n**Status:** Proposed\n\n## Context\n\nWave 1c R0 (ADR-2605250615) established omeprazole enantiomeric separation as the flagship for chiral synthesis, laxative solutions, and cough-expectorant syrups. The R0 scaffold implemented two `pharma_*` cells (`pharma_chiral_resolution`, `pharma_liquid_formulation`) with import-time RuntimeError gating per the silicon Wave 1 pattern.\n\nR1 phase transitions from scaffold to operational readiness by:\n1. Establishing Council Lv6+ ≥3 attestation baseline (`silen-pharma-review` scope: `wave-1c-chiral-resolution-baseline`)\n2. Defining benchtop proof-of-concept (PoC) protocol for omeprazole S-enantiomer separation\n3. Specifying Chiralcel OD-H prep-HPLC column qualification requirements (enantiomeric purity ≥ 99.5%, ICH M7 Class 5)\n4. Documenting benzonatate PMDA jurisdiction margin resolution plan (decision tracking for 2024-2025 approval window)\n5. Detailing cough-expectorant liquid formulation microbial limits and viscosity acceptance criteria (USP <61>/<62>)\n6. Confirming all 14 constitutional gates (G1..G14) + 10 non-goals (N1..N10) remain unchanged — **no constitutional amendment**\n\n## Decision\n\n### 1. Omeprazole Benchtop Synthesis ≤1g Proof-of-Concept Protocol\n\n**Target:** S-enantiomer (omeprazole active form) ≥ 99.5% enantiomeric purity (ICH M7 Class 5 for related substances).\n\n**Two parallel routes qualified at R1:**\n\n#### Route A: Crystalline-Resolution-Mandelate (L-Mandelic Acid Salt)\n\n- **Starting material:** Racemic omeprazole (~0.5 g, Sigma-Aldrich catalog grade, H0891-5G, ≤0.02 EU/mL endotoxin)\n- **Resolving agent:** L(-)-Mandelic acid (≥99% optical purity, Sigma-Aldrich M4256-25G)\n- **Solvent:** Ethyl acetate (≥99.5%, HPLC grade, Fisher Scientific E195-1)\n- **Expected yield:** 65–75% S-enantiomer recovery after salt precipitation and mother-liquor processing\n- **Crystalline monitoring:** Optical rotation [α]₂₀ᴰ (CHCl₃) for S-omeprazole: +52° ± 2° (lit. +50°–+54°); solubility curve (EtOAc 20–40°C) to confirm salt kinetic stability\n- **Enantiomeric purity assay:** Chiralcel OD-H prep-HPLC (see Route B analytics below; minimum one orthogonal method: SFC-supercritical carbon dioxide on Chiralpak IC-3 or equivalent)\n- **Deliverable:** Lot attestation record (`lotAttestation` Lexicon) with `enantiomeric_purity_bp ≥ 9950` (≥99.50%), `recovery_yield_bp 6500–7500` (65–75%), `outcome: \"ok\"` gate\n\n#### Route B: Prep-HPLC-Chiral (Chiralcel OD-H Column)\n\n- **Instrument:** Preparative high-performance liquid chromatography (Agilent 1260 or equivalent), 250 mm × 10 mm I.D. Chiralcel OD-H (5 µm)\n- **Mobile phase:** 80:20 hexane:isopropanol (v/v), 1% TFA (optional; for baseline separation with τ > 1.5), flow rate 4.5 mL/min\n- **Expected resolution:** R_s ≥ 2.5 (baseline separation of S/R enantiomers at ~18 min S, ~25 min R)\n- **Fraction collection:** Automated peak-triggered collection; S-enantiomer window = min 14–22 min (conservative 4-min margin around 18 min apex)\n- **Purity & recovery:** Same targets as Route A (≥99.50% enantiomeric purity, 70–95% overall recovery from racemic feed; typical: 85% for small scale)\n- **Column qualification:** At R1, one 1g loading with recovery + purity attestation; reusability (10-load cycle) deferred to R2 if equipment qualification in-progress\n- **Deliverable:** Same `lotAttestation` record format\n\n**Integration:** Both routes contribute to `pharma_chiral_resolution` cell MST listener trigger on `purificationAttestation` events (scheme: \"crystalline-resolution-mandelate\" | \"prep-hplc-chiral\"). Cell executes PoC protocol, emits `qcAttestation` with `enantiomeric_purity_bp` & `recovery_yield_bp`.\n\n### 2. Council Lv6+ Attestation Baseline: `wave-1c-chiral-resolution-baseline`\n\n**Scope:** Single `silenPharmaReview` NDJSON record with:\n- `scope: \"wave-1c-chiral-resolution-baseline\"`\n- `apiInn: \"omeprazole\"` (singular; extends baseline to cover only omeprazole chiral)\n- `verdict: \"approve\"` (set by Council Lv6+ ≥3 supermajority multisig)\n- `attestationUri: \"at://...did:plc:[council-multisig-actor]/com.etzhayyim.pharma.silenPharmaReview/...\"` (published via `council.etzhayyim.com` Bluesky PDS)\n\n**Gate unlock condition:** Both `COUNCIL_ATTESTATION_TX_HASH` (Base L2 Council Lv6+ multisig Tx hash) and `SILEN_PHARMA_BASELINE_REVIEW_CID` (IPFS CID of above record) set non-None in `pharma_chiral_resolution/cell.py` + `pharma_liquid_formulation/cell.py`.\n\n**Timing:** Must land **before** R2 pilot phase (≤100g synthesis). Proposed timeline: Council motion during 2026-05 meeting; execution by 2026-06-30.\n\n### 3. Cough-Expectorant Liquid Formulation (Guaifenesin + Benzonatate)\n\n**Scope:** `pharma_liquid_formulation` cell, triggered on `fillFinishAttestation` with `dosageForm` in [\"oral-liquid-syrup\", \"oral-suspension\"].\n\n**Guaifenesin 100 mg/5 mL Syrup:**\n- **Excipients:** Sorbitol solution 70% (humectant), glycerin (solvent), sodium benzoate 0.1% w/v (preservative — exception per G3 note below), FD&C Yellow #6 (colorant), flavor compound (lime / cherry), purified water\n- **pH:** 5.2–6.0 (DeciUnits 52–60)\n- **Viscosity:** 50–80 milli-centipoise @ 25°C (MilliCp 50–80)\n- **Microbial limits (USP <61>/<62>):** aerobic bacteria ≤10⁴ CFU/mL, fungi ≤10² CFU/mL; *E. coli*, *S. aureus*, *P. aeruginosa* absent in 10 mL\n- **Dissolution:** Not applicable (solute already dissolved)\n- **QC frequency:** Each 5L batch fill\n\n**Benzonatate 100–150 mg/5 mL Suspension:**\n- **Formulation challenge:** Benzonatate is lipophilic (log P ~3.5); suspends in glycerin-based vehicle (not freely soluble)\n- **Excipients:** Glycerin (suspending vehicle), xanthan gum (thickener), sodium benzoate 0.1% (preservative), FD&C Red #40, flavor, purified water\n- **Viscosity:** 100–150 milli-centipoise @ 25°C (MilliCp 100–150)\n- **Particle size:** ≤5 µm median (laser diffraction; Sympatec or equivalent)\n- **Microbial limits:** Same as guaifenesin (USP <61>/<62>)\n- **Resuspendability:** After 4-week settle test @ 25°C/60% RH, <5 min hand-shake resuspension to homogeneity\n- **QC frequency:** Each 5L batch fill\n\n**G3 preservative exception note:** Sodium benzoate 0.1% is permitted under G3 interim (pending Council review of safer alternatives: potassium sorbate, glycerin + low-pH combo). Amendment via dedicated ADR if replacement approved.\n\n**Deliverable:** `fillFinishAttestation` + `qcAttestation` records with microbial + viscosity pass/fail, triggering `pharma_liquid_formulation` cell verdict on intake.\n\n### 4. Benzonatate PMDA Jurisdiction Margin\n\n**Current status:** Benzonatate is OTC in USA (Tessalon cough drop, ParexelOTC) and EMA (approved via decentralized procedure), but Japan has Rx form (Besibun liquid for prescription-only) and OTC proposal submitted to PMDA around 2023.\n\n**Decision:** R1 phase **does NOT** manufacture or distribute benzonatate pending PMDA decision. Instead:\n1. **Monitoring window:** Track PMDA official decision announcement (expected 2024–2025, per published PMDA review timelines)\n2. **R1.5 contingency:** If PMDA approves OTC by 2026-06-30, issue R1.5 amendment ADR (`ADR-2605250645`) to unlock `pharma_liquid_formulation` for benzonatate ≥100 mg/5 mL\n3. **R1.5 fallback:** If PMDA does NOT approve OTC by 2026-06-30, benzonatate stays in Wave 2 carve-out (separate master charter, higher scrutiny required)\n4. **Monitoring owner:** yakushi QA lead (responsibility: quarterly check of PMDA official journal + news alerts; escalate to Council Lv6+ if surprise approval/denial)\n\n**Implication:** Guaifenesin syrup is R1-ready now; benzonatate suspension manufacturing remains blocked until R1.5 decision lands.\n\n### 5. Inheritance of Constitutional Gates & Non-Goals\n\n**No amendment to 14 gates (G1..G14) or 10 non-goals (N1..N10) from ADR-2605250615.**\n\n- **G1–G6:** OTC scope, off-patent, ICH compliance, Council attestation, witness, non-controlled — all unchanged, all met by omeprazole + guaifenesin + benzonatate (if approved)\n- **G7:** CWC Schedule 3 precursor check — omeprazole route uses NO OPCW-scheduled reagents (contrast Wave 1b analgesics using acetic anhydride) — **CLEAR**\n- **G8–G14:** Sterile facility, witness N≥2, XChaCha20 AE, wellbecoming label, no-commercial-sale, no-server-key, inference-Murakumo-only — all inherited, all enforced at cell entry via gates\n\n**Non-goals N1..N10 also inherited:** no NME, no Rx-only, no biologic, no commercial model, no advertising, no patent fence, no insurance gate, no animal testing, no frontier LLM, no vendor revenue — confirmed for all APIs in scope.\n\n## Consequences\n\n### Timing\n\n- **2026-05 (this month):** Council motion for `wave-1c-chiral-resolution-baseline` attestation + benzonatate PMDA monitoring assignment\n- **2026-06-30 (deadline):** Gate unlock (COUNCIL_ATTESTATION_TX_HASH + CID set) OR R1.5 amendment issue if benzonatate PMDA decision arrives\n- **2026-07 (R2 phase):** Pilot ≤100g synthesis with Annex 1 facility + QP on-site; 3-batch media fill for sterile dosages\n\n### Operational Impact\n\n1. **pharma_chiral_resolution cell:** Transitions from `raise RuntimeError(...)` to executable PoC runner once gates are set\n2. **pharma_liquid_formulation cell:** Guaifenesin branch active; benzonatate branch conditional on R1.5\n3. **MST listener:** Subscriptions to `purificationAttestation` (chiral) + `fillFinishAttestation` (liquid) activate; cell publishes `qcAttestation` records\n4. **Witness dispatch:** Operator DID + QP-equivalent DID (or automated sensor DID) signature requirement enforced; N=1 escalates to Council via MstListener hook\n\n### Risk & Mitigation\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|\n| Council attestation delayed past 2026-06-30 | Defer R2 pilot by 1 month; stretch timeline to 2026-08 |\n| Benzonatate PMDA approval arrives mid-2026-06 | Issue R1.5 amendment ADR within 5 days; PR gate-unlock to main by 2026-06-15 contingency |\n| Chiralcel OD-H column damages during prep-HPLC | Stock 2nd column as cold spare; ramp-down to Route A (crystalline-resolution) until repair/replacement (4-week lead time) |\n| Omeprazole ≤1g PoC yields <65% (below threshold) | Investigate salt-crystal kinetics; switch to Route B prep-HPLC; document failure analysis for Council R1.5 review |\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### 1. Single Route Only (Route A or Route B)\n**Rejected.** Two parallel routes de-risk equipment failure and provide redundancy for Council review. Benchtop PoC with both routes demonstrates process flexibility at scale-up.\n\n### 2. Skip Benzonatate Until R2\n**Rejected for current language; accepted as contingency.** R1 includes guaifenesin syrup immediately; benzonatate suspension timing pegged to PMDA jurisdiction decision, not Council discretion. Monitoring assignment is explicit R1 deliverable.\n\n### 3. SFC-Supercritical Carbon Dioxide as Primary Route\n**Rejected.** Route B (prep-HPLC Chiralcel OD-H) is literature-standard for omeprazole; SFC is orthogonal confirmatory assay at R1 only. SFC upscale (pilot ≤100g) deferred to R2 if yield advantage demonstrated.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2605250500: yakushi pharmaceutical R&D charter (master 14 gates + 10 non-goals)\n- ADR-2605250615: yakushi Wave 1c R0 scaffold (omeprazole, laxatives, cough-expectorant)\n- ADR-2605181100: XChaCha20-Poly1305 confidentiality (patient AE envelope)\n- ADR-2605231525: no-server-key invariant (G13 enforcement, passkey + hardware token only)\n- ICH M7 Guideline: Assessment and Control of DNA Reactive (Genotoxic) Impurities in Pharmaceuticals to Limit Potential Health Risk (Class 5 = related substance <0.5% of IMP)\n- USP <61> Microbiological Examination of Nonsterile Products: Tests for Specified Microorganisms (aerobic bacteria, fungi, *E. coli*, *S. aureus*, *P. aeruginosa*)\n- USP <62> Microbiological Tests – Tests for Specified Microorganisms in Pharmaceutical Products (limit testing protocol)\n- PMDA Japanese Pharmacopoeia OTC Status Review (2023–2025 window; benzonatate decision tracking)\n- Sigma-Aldrich catalog: H0891-5G (racemic omeprazole), M4256-25G (L-mandelic acid), E195-1 (ethyl acetate HPLC)\n- Agilent 1260 Infinity II Preparative HPLC System (Chiralcel OD-H 250×10 mm I.D., 5 µm)\n- Sympatec HELOS(H) Laser Diffraction (particle size ≤5 µm benzonatate suspension)\n\n---\n\n**ADR Status:** Proposed (awaiting Council motion 2026-05).\n**Next Action:** Circulate to Council Lv6+ for ballot; cross-reference in `deps.toml` [[adrs]].\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605250630-yakushi-wave-1c-r1-chiral-commissioning.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "yakushi/pharmaceutical/chiral-synthesis", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-25T00:00:00Z", :adr/date "2026-05-25T00:00:00Z", :adr/authoritative true}]
